# [[ .Name ]]-quanar

The quanar: sign-in, the dashboard and the quan loader. It holds no business logic.

| Folder | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `constants` | values: API endpoints, routes, storage keys, delivery descriptions, demo users |
| `config` | settings, the code side of `.env`, and the quans the server does not know (`static-quans`) |
| `core` | mechanisms: `axios-client` (the axios instance and `httpClient`: get, post, put, patch, delete), `auth-manager`, `quan-loader`, `sse-client`, `qua-core`, `navigation` |
| `api` | requests, made with the core's axios client |
| `store` | zustand stores: `auth-store`, `quan-store`, `ui-store` |
| `services` | where api, core, utils and stores meet: auth, quans, the qua, notifications, navigation |
| `hooks` | call services only; each file holds its context, provider and hook |
| `pages` | use hooks and components only |
| `components`, `layouts`, `router`, `utils`, `types`, `langs`, `assets` | the rest |

The quan loader fetches a quan's build, and when its source carries a hash
(every quan registered in the server does), compares the SHA-256 of the file
with it before running it. `quaService.plug()` implements every call of the qua
with the quanar's services, `http` being `httpClient` itself: a quan's `api`
folder calls `http.get` and `http.post` from the qua and its requests leave
through the quanar's axios client with the user's token. Quans reach the quanar
through nothing else.
